rezono 0
pack subsidy-scheme

rules costs
  | // What an application costs: the lines of its quotes, their total, and the part the regulation counts.
  | // Soufflé syntax, so Soufflé is the oracle. The base relations are the tables of the schema:
  | // `k(id)` per kind and `k__a(id, v)` per arrow or attribute. Amounts are whole cents.
  | 
  | // A quote line with its application, its cost item and its amount.
  | .decl line(application: symbol, cost_line: symbol, item: symbol, cents: number)
  | line(a, l, i, c) :- cost_line__application(l, a), cost_line__item(l, i), cost_line__amount(l, c).
  | 
  | // An application with at least one quote line. Without one there is no total: unknown is not zero.
  | .decl has_quote(application: symbol)
  | has_quote(a) :- line(a, _, _, _).
  | 
  | // What the quotes of an application add up to.
  | .decl quoted_costs(application: symbol, cents: number)
  | quoted_costs(a, t) :- has_quote(a), t = sum c : { line(a, _, _, c) }.
  | 
  | // A line whose cost item the regulation counts (article 3), and what those lines add up to.
  | .decl eligible_line(application: symbol, cost_line: symbol, cents: number)
  | eligible_line(a, l, c) :- line(a, l, i, c), cost_item__eligibility(i, "eligible").
  | 
  | .decl eligible_costs(application: symbol, cents: number)
  | eligible_costs(a, t) :- has_quote(a), t = sum c : { eligible_line(a, _, c) }.
  | 
  | // Invariant: the costs on the application form equal the total of the quotes. The two come from different
  | // documents, so a difference, even of one cent, means a quote is missing or was entered wrongly. It blocks
  | // publication until it is repaired.
  | // @invariant
  | .decl costs_mismatch(application: symbol, claimed: number, quoted: number)
  | costs_mismatch(a, x, q) :- quoted_costs(a, q), application__claimed_costs(a, x), x != q.
  | 
  | .output quoted_costs, eligible_costs, costs_mismatch
